Aim:
To execute queries using set operators and special conditions in Oracle.

Algorithm:
1. Create two tables.
2. Insert sample records.
3. Execute queries using ANY, ALL, IN, EXISTS, and NOT EXISTS.
4. Perform UNION and INTERSECT.
5. Display the results.

Program:
-- ANY
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE SALARY > ANY (
    SELECT SALARY FROM EMPLOYEE
    WHERE DEPARTMENT = 'HR'
);
-- ALL
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE SALARY > ALL (
    SELECT SALARY FROM EMPLOYEE
    WHERE DEPARTMENT = 'HR'
);
-- IN
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE DEPARTMENT IN ('IT', 'HR');
-- EXISTS
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE E
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM EMPLOYEE X
    WHERE X.EMP_ID = E.EMP_ID
);
-- NOT EXISTS
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE E
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM EMPLOYEE X
    WHERE X.EMP_ID = E.EMP_ID
    AND X.SALARY > 30000
);
-- UNION
SELECT EMP_NAME FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE DEPARTMENT = 'IT'
UNION
SELECT EMP_NAME FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE DEPARTMENT = 'HR';
-- INTERSECT
SELECT EMP_NAME FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE SALARY >= 25000
INTERSECT
SELECT EMP_NAME FROM EMPLOYEE
WHERE SALARY <= 30000;

Result:
Queries using set operators and special conditions were executed successfully.
